  "Born Elizabeth Mackintosh at Inverness on 25 July 1896; she trained as a physical education teacher and wrote under the name Gordon Daviot for the stage and Josephine Tey for her crime novels. The Franchise Affair (1948), The Daughter of Time (1951) and Brat Farrar (1949) followed, with the play Richard of Bordeaux (1933). She died in London on 13 February 1952.",
