  "Writer and Irish nationalist; the author of The Riddle of the Sands, the first modern spy novel.",
  "Born Robert Erskine Childers in London on 25 June 1870; he served in the Boer War, wrote The Riddle of the Sands in 1903, ran guns to Ireland in the Asgard in 1914, and became a minister in the Irish Free State. He was executed by the Free State government on 24 November 1922.",
